#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Question]
#v(40pt)
If the price of good X decreases, what happens to the quantity demanded of good X due to the substitution effect?
#v(20pt)
a) Increases
#v(10pt)
b) Decreases
#only("1")[
#voiceover("Not quite. Let's see the correct solution.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Step 1: Understand the Substitution Effect 🔄]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Substitution effect: change in consumption due to change in relative prices, holding utility constant]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("The substitution effect represents the change in consumption of a good when its price changes, while holding the consumer's utility or satisfaction constant.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Step 2: Analyze Price Decrease 📉]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- When the price of good X decreases, it becomes relatively cheaper compared to other goods]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("In this case, the price of good X decreases. This makes good X relatively cheaper compared to other goods.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Step 3: Determine the Effect on Quantity Demanded 📈]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Consumers will substitute away from other goods and towards good X]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- This leads to an increase in the quantity demanded of good X]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("As a result, consumers will tend to substitute away from other goods and buy more of good X.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("This substitution towards good X leads to an increase in the quantity demanded of good X.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Conclusion]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- The substitution effect causes the quantity demanded of good X to increase when its price decreases 📊]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("In conclusion, due to the substitution effect, when the price of good X decreases, the quantity demanded of good X will increase.")
]
]